discovered_objects.exact_quotation:
Define a candidate carrier:

\[
\mathcal M=(L,T,\vdash,\mathsf{Comp},X,\Sigma,E,R),
\]

where:

- \(L\) is an object language;
- \(T\) is an effectively presented theory;
- \(\vdash\) is its proof relation;
- \(\mathsf{Comp}\) is its modeled computational dynamics;
- \(X\) is its physical state space;
- \(\Sigma\) is its entropy or thermodynamic state description;
- \(E\) is its available energy/free-energy account;
- \(R\) is its physically instantiated record structure.
